@startuml
title T12 — Shared n8n Error Handler (Separate Workflow; Not Counted in 12 Nodes)
autonumber
participant "n8n Business Workflow" as SOURCE
participant "n8n Error Handler\n(Error Trigger)" as ERR
participant "NestJS Backend" as API
database "PostgreSQL" as DB
participant "Notification Service" as NOTIFY

SOURCE -> ERR: n8n execution failed (workflowId, executionId, lastNode, error)
activate ERR
ERR -> ERR: Normalize error event and derive correlation ID
ERR -> ERR: Redact tokens, passwords, PII and secret-bearing request headers
ERR -> API: POST workflow failure callback
API -> DB: Idempotently record WorkflowRun failure / AuditLog entry
DB --> API: Recorded status and correlation reference
API --> ERR: Failure record accepted
alt Critical failure or repeated delivery failure
ERR -> API: Request idempotent in-app notification
API -> NOTIFY: Notify owner/maintainer with sanitized diagnostic summary
NOTIFY --> API: Notification status
API --> ERR: Notification accepted/failed
else Non-critical failure
ERR -> ERR: Keep sanitized failure record without noisy notification
end
opt Retry policy explicitly permits automatic retry
ERR -> API: Request retry/reschedule through backend policy
API -> DB: Record retry attempt and next-run state
DB --> API: Retry state
API --> ERR: Retry scheduled or rejected
end
deactivate ERR
note over SOURCE,ERR
This is a separate Error Trigger workflow. It is not one of the 15 business
workflows and does not count toward their 12 functional nodes. Prevent the
error handler from recursively invoking itself; store sanitized diagnostics only.
end note
@enduml
